8530	{"artifactId":"LLD-6a811b8acca60ac5-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-6a811b8acca60ac5-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-12T05:47:20.480Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"fix-targets-defect.1","ref":"fix-targets-defect","item":"fix-targets-defect","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design covers every clause of the ISSUE's fix intent: only one request is actionable at a time (only the head is shown and accepted), a follow-up is never cut short by a later approval (one follow-up per batch, run only after the turn ends and every request is decided), deny has a visible effect (rejected chip, follow-up names it as denied, all-denied gives a notice), grants accumulate (grant chain), both paths are handled (turn-ended batch and in-turn decide() relay), there is one outcome row per decision in order, and single-request behaviour is unchanged.","evidence":"ISSUE-6a811b8acca60ac5 fixIntent requires: one actionable request at a time; 'a follow-up turn started by an approval is never cancelled by a later approval'; deny with a 'defined, visible effect'; approved grants 'still in force'; both approval paths; outcome chips 'one per decision and in the order'; dir-block and exact-command behaviour unchanged. The LLD covers each one in 2.2/2.3/3.1 and in its edge-case table. The ISSUE's root cause says runTurn calls cancelActive(). That is stale: the current code supersedes through turns.start's newest-message-wins (chat-panel.ts:677-680). The LLD correctly targets the real mechanism. [files: .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-6a811b8acca60ac5.json, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today every approval-request that carries a toolName goes into pendingPerms and is posted at once. Each Approve immediately calls runTurn with only that one tool allowed, and turns.start's newest-message-wins supersedes a running follow-up without killing its process.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:647-659: onEvent posts every event, then `if (ev.kind === 'approval-request' && typeof ev.toolName === 'string' && ev.toolName !== '') pendingPerms.set(...)`. :833/:836 `void runTurn(..., [pending.toolName], { suppressEcho: true })`. turn-lifecycle.ts:221-227 `waitCtl?.abort(); const myGen = ++generation;` and :331-342: a superseded turn keeps being read but reports nothing more ('The previous turn's process is NOT killed'). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"In-turn requests usually carry a toolName too, so routing has to use the new resolution field rather than whether a toolName is present.","evidence":"cli-adapter.ts:309,318: normalizeApprovalEvent sets toolName from APPROVAL_TOOL_KEYS whenever one is found. chat-panel.ts:653 only tests toolName, so today such an in-turn request is caught by the pendingPerms grant path and never relayed with decide(). Only toolName-less requests reach decide() (test comment at chat-panel.test.ts:1956). The LLD's resolution-based routing correctly fixes this misrouting. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"There are two places where approval-requests are produced: claude's inline system/permission_denied branch (to be marked 'turn-ended') and the shared normalizeApprovalEvent (to be marked 'in-turn'), which serves both claude's control-protocol branch and codex. Marking these two covers every producer.","evidence":"Grep finds only two `kind: 'approval-request'` literals in non-test code: cli-adapter.ts:313 (normalizeApprovalEvent) and :538 (the permission_denied branch at :519-546). normalizeApprovalEvent is called at :624 (claude control_request / permission_request / can_use_tool) and :682 (codex approval item). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/cli-adapter.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The host change sites are complete. Besides runTurn's TurnSink, followLiveTurn's FollowSink posts turn-events directly, and the webview bootstrap at chat-panel.ts:514 builds the approval card meta. Both are listed for change, as is postInitialState.","evidence":"chat-panel.ts:247-256: followLiveTurn onEvent does `post({ type: 'turn-event', event: ev })`, which would bypass the queue if left alone; the LLD covers it in 2.4. :514 `reg.renderRow({kind:'approval',...,meta:{requestId:ev.requestId,title:ev.title,detail:ev.detail,toolName:ev.toolName}})` has no position/total; the LLD adds them in 2.6/3.2. :258-272 postInitialState re-runs on every 'ready' (:729). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.1","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"An approval-request is live-only: it is never written as a transcript row and never replayed on restore. Only permission-outcome rows persist, through recordPermissionOutcome.","evidence":"markers.ts:84-86 `case 'approval-request': ... never persisted (k4)` returns null, so appendEvent (chat-panel.ts:708-713) writes no row for it. markers.ts:139 does the same in the webview. chat-panel.ts:214-221: recordPermissionOutcome posts the chip and pushes `{ role: 'permission-outcome', toolName, decision }`. The queue only delays posting and never persists the request, so the invariant holds. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/markers.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"preserved-behaviour.2","ref":"preserved-behaviour","item":"preserved-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A batch can be ended reliably on the turn's terminal event reaching onEvent: done or error is delivered to sink.onEvent before onTerminal, and an output that ends with no terminal event is turned into an error event.","evidence":"turn-lifecycle.ts:343-348: `sink.onEvent(ev); if (isTerminal(ev)) { endTurn(ev, it); sink.onTerminal(ev) }`. :310-321: when the output ends with no done/error, it synthesizes `{ kind: 'error', ..., message: 'the CLI ended without finishing the turn' }` and passes it to onEvent and onTerminal. Superseded, aborted or detached turns return without onTerminal (:292, :309), which the LLD handles explicitly (Stop clears, detach drops, supersede only after a user-typed submit clears). [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/turn-lifecycle.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing chat-panel test harness can carry the planned acceptance tests: a fake provider that scripts approval-request events and records decide() calls, so each multi-request test (head-only card, one follow-up per batch, deny, decide-before-next) would fail against today's code.","evidence":"chat-panel.test.ts:53 `onDecide?: (turnId, requestId, decision) => void; // S004: decide() relay`. Scripted approval-request events appear at :1581, :1774-2058, including toolName/command/dir-block variants. Today all cards are posted at once (chat-panel.ts:648) and each Approve calls runTurn right away (:833/:836). So 'only the first card is posted', 'turns.start is called once per batch' and 'decide() for the first before the second card' all fail without the fix. Every ac1-ac6 maps to at least one such test. [files: vscode-plugin/src/chat/__tests__/chat-panel.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/chat/chat-panel.ts]","action":"none","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":8,"unverified":0},"template":"design-issue","reviewedAt":"2026-10-12T05:47:20.480Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
